{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"81bd81a9-ceef-4078-af48-fdd9929ac431","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have run the 10 read-only checks against [server.py](file:///tmp/h-ryTIg3/server.py) on port `50277` and written the full report to [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-ryTIg3/ANSWER.md) without modifying any existing files.\n\n### Summary of Findings (`has the problem`)\n\n- **C1 (`PASS`, with `resources/list` caveat):** `initialize`, `tools/list` (3 tools), and `server/discover` (`-32601`) all succeed without a token (`HTTP 200`). *(Note: `initialize` advertises `capabilities.resources`, but calling `resources/list` without a token returns `HTTP 401` `{\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}` at [`handle`](file:///tmp/h-ryTIg3/server.py#L148-L150).)*\n- **C2 (`FAIL`):** Calling [`call_tool`](file:///tmp/h-ryTIg3/server.py#L113-L120) / [`handle`](file:///tmp/h-ryTIg3/server.py#L161-L164) on `get_note` with a non-existent ID (`{\"id\": \"n-999\"}`) or missing required argument (`{}`) returns a JSON-RPC `-32602` error instead of a tool result with `isError: true` — Fix: [My live MCP test asserted the bug: a real client threw where my test passed](https://worklore.dev/s/2026-10-02-my-live-mcp-test-asserted-the-bug-a-real-client-threw-where-).\n- **C3 (`PASS`):** The session (`Mcp-Session-Id`) survives the C2 errors and returns a normal `get_note` result immediately afterward.\n- **C4 (`PASS`):** Both read-only tools (`get_note` and `search_notes`) return `isError: false` and `structuredContent` matching their published `outputSchema`.\n- **C5 (`PASS`):** All responses parse cleanly as JSON with no encoder/`Decimal` errors and proper integer types (`words`, `total`).\n- **C6 (`FAIL` / `WARN`):** The server (`notes-mcp` `0.3.1`, surface hash `sha256:4d069975b7acb158f2f12ceb8c69abeb4fd1569723f844bcab6988682a982d03`) has no committed surface lock file or test in the repository and is not yet listed in the MCP Registry — Fix: [My MCP listing said read-only. My server could write.](https://worklore.dev/s/2026-09-30-my-mcp-listing-said-read-only-my-server-could-write) and [Getting into the MCP Registry](https://worklore.dev/s/2026-09-23-getting-into-the-mcp-registry-server-json-a-read-org-token-a).\n- **C7 (`PASS`):** [`log`](file:///tmp/h-ryTIg3/server.py#L80-L83) in [`Handler.do_POST`](file:///tmp/h-ryTIg3/server.py#L216) writes one structured JSON line per call (`t`, `method`, `tool`, `ok`, `ms`, `who`) to `stderr`, including errors.\n- **C8 (`PASS`):** All 3 tool names (`search_notes`, `get_note`, `add_note`) match `^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{1,64}$`.\n- **C9 (`PASS`):** `initialize` with `\"protocolVersion\": \"banana\"` responds with `\"protocolVersion\": \"2025-06-18\"`.\n- **C10 (`FAIL`):** While `get_note` and `add_note` reject corrupted payloads, `search_notes` declares `\"outputSchema\": {\"type\": \"object\"}` ([`TOOLS`](file:///tmp/h-ryTIg3/server.py#L34)), which has no required fields or constraints and accepts the corrupted payload `{}` — Fix: [My MCP server's output schemas accepted wrong answers](https://worklore.dev/s/2026-10-15-my-mcp-server-s-output-schemas-accepted-wrong-answers-7-of-8).\n","duration_seconds":385.976578,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":64713,"output_tokens":28971,"thinking_tokens":19738,"cache_read_tokens":403618,"total_tokens":93684}}}
